 Before using passes, I'll do a free weight-only scan for structural anomalies that could make copying too strong. In the full-attention layers I'll check q_norm/k_norm gains (these set attention sharpness and so the strength of exact-match copying) and per-head v/o norms. In the DeltaNet layers I'll check decay parameters (A_log, dt_bias). For the MLPs I'll look for outlier neurons by down_proj norm. A single out-of-family value (one layer's k_norm far larger than the others, say) would be a strong lead. A smooth profile would mean the loops are the model's intrinsic behaviour under these sampling settings, and I would localize from activations instead.\n\n```python\n# Weight scan for anomalies: q/k norm gains, per-head o/v norms (full attn), A_log/dt_bias (DeltaNet), MLP neuron outliers\nimport torch\nP='model.language_model.layers.'\nfor l in [3,7,11,15,19,23]:\n    qn=load(P+f'{l}.self_attn.q_norm.weight'); kn=load(P+f'{l}.self_attn.k_norm.weight')\n    o=load(P+f'{l}.self_attn.o_proj.weight'); v=load(P+f'{l}.self_attn.v_proj.weight'); q=load(P+f'{l}.self_attn.q_proj.weight')\n    on=o.view(1024,8,256).norm(dim=(0,2)); vn=v.view(2,256,1024).norm(dim=(1,2))\n    print(l,'q_norm mean/max %.2f/%.2f'%(qn.mean(),qn.abs().max()),'k_norm mean/max %.2f/%.2f'%(kn.mean(),kn.abs().max()),\n          'q_proj',tuple(q.shape),'o head norms',np.round(on.numpy(),1),'v kv-head norms',np.round(vn.numpy(),1))\n```","ttft_ms":75952,"type":"result","duration_ms":83068,"uuid":"d8a1ab1b-435b-4022-8179-169f9ac76478","ttft_stream_ms":1208,"time_to_request_ms":297,"first_content_frame_ms":1208,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":7737,"cacheReadInputTokens":41373,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1437,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.17452659999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":6984,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":1437,"canoni